license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - agent evaluation
  - benchmark
  - financial decision making
  - event stream
  - time and state
  - look-ahead prevention
  - SEC filings
  - LLM agents
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for AI agents that must make timely, auditable decisions over continuously updating
  financial data streams. One case is one continuous duty shift: filings, margin calls, payment
  notices and market data are released on a business clock; agents must forecast, reconcile, verify
  and act before each window closes, and an offline deterministic judge re-computes the frozen
  evidence. The flagship case reconstructs Alphabet's Q1 2026 earnings night from real SEC EDGAR
  filings and prices, with database-level publication-time gating (available_at_s) and a
  nine-metric pre-earnings forecast. v1.4.0 applies a validity-first scoring refactor (rebalanced
  weights, bounded Brier Skill Score, per-submission audit, reconciliation self-consistency, and
  evidence/logic/handover LLM rubrics). Measured difficulty with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash: six scored
  rollouts, mean 43.14 +- 5.61 (final configuration four runs: 42.01 +- 1.50); the same evidence
  under the previous v1.3.1 weights scores mean 36.40, showing the shift is from weight
  reallocation, not criterion loosening. Cross-model evaluation (3 rollouts each, same task package
  and judge): DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash mean 46.83 +- 3.72, DeepSeek-V4-Pro mean 32.48 +- 1.96; the gap
  concentrates in the analysis-quality rubrics, and the rubrics were calibrated on Flash traces, so
  a style bias caveat is documented.
